  "id": "muliza_pasco",
  "name": "Muliza (Pasco and Tarma carnival song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The muliza is a carnival song-dance of Peru's central highlands, strongest in Cerro de Pasco and Tarma, whose name and lore tie it to the muleteers who drove mule trains through the region. It is sung to estudiantina string bands of mandolins, guitars and violins or to orquestas típicas with saxophones, clarinets, violin and harp, and it accompanies the carnival comparsas.",
  "recipe": "classic modern muliza, carnival Processional, andean branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. mandolin, classical nylon-string guitar, fiddle, saxophone, clarinet, arpa peruana. mountain valley. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
